# Suppressions for `trivy config modules/`.
#
# Every entry carries a reason and an expiry. Trivy enforces the expiry: on the
# date below the finding comes back, the test in
# packages/emitters/terraform/src/modules.test.ts fails, and someone has to
# either fix the module or renew the entry with a fresh justification. A
# suppression nobody revisits is a finding that was deleted rather than
# handled.
#
# The reasoning also lives next to the resource it applies to. This file is the
# list; the module says why.

# AZU-0013 — Key Vault has no deny-by-default network ACL.
#
# Two things that must reach the vault sit outside any network we control:
# Terraform writing the generated Postgres credentials from a GitHub-hosted
# runner or the direct executor, neither of which has a stable address; and
# Container Apps resolving a secret reference at revision start-up, which is
# not on Key Vault's trusted-services list, so `bypass = "AzureServices"` does
# not cover it. Closing the vault stops apps from starting.
#
# Deny-by-default needs a private endpoint and a vault-scoped subnet, which is
# separate work with its own cost. The gate until then is RBAC: no access
# policies, Secrets User for apps, Secrets Officer only for the deploying
# principal. `var.network_acls` is there for an operator who has done the
# private-endpoint work.
#
# See modules/azure-keyvault/README.md.
AVD-AZU-0013 exp:2027-03-01
